#: ../doc/export.rst:158
msgid "Export Complete"
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/export.rst:160
msgid "When an export finishes, a :guilabel:`Complete` tab opens in the Export window (unless :guilabel:`Show Export Dialog when Finished` is turned off in :ref:`preferences_ref`). It shows where the file was saved, with a button to copy its path, along with a summary of the export: format, resolution, quality, file size, duration, and how long the export took."
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/export.rst:165
msgid ":guilabel:`Watch Video` opens the exported file in your default video player (:guilabel:`Play Audio` for audio-only exports)."
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/export.rst:167
msgid ":guilabel:`Open Containing Folder` opens your file manager with the exported file selected."
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/export.rst:169
msgid "The `Simple` and `Advanced` tabs are still available, but read-only, so you can review exactly which settings were used. Click :guilabel:`Done` to close the window."
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/export.rst:172
msgid "If an export fails, an :guilabel:`Export Failed` tab explains what went wrong. :guilabel:`Copy Error Details` copies the error and export settings (helpful when reporting a problem), and :guilabel:`Try Again` reopens the Export window with the same settings."
msgstr ""

#: ../doc/export.rst:176
msgid "A successful export also fires a burst of confetti. Use the :guilabel:`Celebrate Exports` preference to show it on the first export only (the default), on every export, or never."
msgstr ""

